cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Observatoire Laudisi: a continuous multimodal observatory of
  French rolling-news television
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it using the metadata
  in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: de Boisvilliers
    given-names: Yann
    affiliation: Université Paris-Dauphine–PSL / EHESS
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
abstract: >-
  Observatoire Laudisi is a research instrument that has
  captured, transcribed and analysed France's three
  rolling-news channels (BFMTV, CNews, France Info)
  continuously since March 2026. Spoken word, speaker
  identity and on-screen text are aligned on a single
  timeline, supporting the study of agenda convergence
  between channels, framing divergence at constant topic,
  and the circadian structure of continuous news
  programming.
keywords:
  - computational social science
  - media sociology
  - television news
  - agenda setting
  - multimodal corpora
license: CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
date-released: '2026-09-11'
version: '1.0'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Yanndebois974/laudisi_observatory'
